2. What changed: [js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L288](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773935668545-11208/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L288) now buckets emitted messages directly from worker results and records touched partitions in the same pass. [js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L625](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773935668545-11208/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L625) now uses that single-pass result inside `_stepParallel`, removing the repeated `flatMap` allocation and the extra bucket scan. No protected engines or non-allowed files were touched.

3. Focused verification run: `node --check js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js` passed. I also ran a targeted Node microbenchmark of the replaced aggregation path; on a synthetic boundary-heavy workload it went from about `922ms` to `382ms` over `50,000` iterations. Full `quick`/`standard` strict parity and end-to-end benchmark verification are left to the runner, per your prompt.

